    label_top: 0
sources:
    - id: owid_ods
      title: Emissions of ozone-depleting substances
      authors: Our World in Data, from the UN Environment Programme (2023)
      year: 2023
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/ozone-depleting-substance-consumption
      finding: 'world consumption of ozone-depleting substances, in ODP tonnes: about 1.66 million in 1989 and about 17,000 in 2021'
    - id: owid_ozone
      title: The world has made great progress in cutting the use of substances that deplete the ozone layer
      authors: Hannah Ritchie, Lucas Rodés-Guirao and Max Roser (Our World in Data)
      year: 2023
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/ozone-layer
      finding: global emissions of ozone-depleting substances have fallen by more than 99% since 1989; the ozone hole stopped growing around 2000
    - id: unep
      title: Ozone layer recovery is on track (Scientific Assessment of Ozone Depletion 2022)
      authors: UN Environment Programme / Scientific Assessment Panel to the Montreal Protocol
      year: 2023
      url: https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc
      finding: ozone back to 1980 levels by about 2040 for most of the world and about 2066 over Antarctica

    dot endpt #b5482e at.data [2021,17] hidden true
    text drop "−99%" #b5482e at.data [2012,700] cites ["owid_ozone"] font_size 90 hidden true
    text montreal "← Montreal treaty" #2f6b8f at.data [1999,1640] cites ["owid_ozone"] font_size 44 hidden true
    text every "every country signed" #2f6b8f at.data [2004,1400] font_size 44 hidden true
    scale tl cites ["unep"] x 90 y 360 width 840 font_size 34 min 1980 max 2070 hidden true
    text now "today ↓" #5e584e x 559.3333333333333 y 510 font_size 36 hidden true
    path brace thick #b5482e points [[519.3333333333333,285],[519.3333333333333,270],[892.6666666666666,270],[892.6666666666666,285]] hidden true
    text yrs40 "40 more years" #b5482e cites ["unep"] x 706 y 230 font_size 50 hidden true
    icon holeic size 150 set twemoji x 166.66666666666666 y 590 icon_look picture of "globe showing americas" hidden true
    path mt1 thick #5e584e points [[136.66666666666666,360],[136.66666666666666,280]] hidden true
    text ml1 "1985: hole found" #5e584e x 246.66666666666666 y 250 font_size 40 hidden true
    path mt2 thick #2f6b8f points [[276.66666666666663,360],[276.66666666666663,410]] hidden true
    text ml2 "2000: stops growing" #2f6b8f x 276.66666666666663 y 435 font_size 40 hidden true
    path mt3 thick #b5482e points [[892.6666666666666,360],[892.6666666666666,410]] hidden true
    text ml3 "2066: healed" #b5482e x 832.6666666666666 y 435 font_size 40 hidden true

    card title "Ozone-killing gases: what next?"

What happened to the gases that eat the ozone layer, once the world agreed to ban them?
    draw axes line_1

    ask "Draw the line on to 2021." on line_1 from 1989 store g after keep
        default: 1500,1350,1200,1050,900,800,700,600,500,450,400
        intro: In 1989 the world used more than one and a half million tonnes a year.
        right: Close. It really did crash almost to the floor.
        wrong: Steeper than that. The line drops almost to the floor.

    animate stage 1 duration 2

By 2021 it was about seventeen thousand tonnes: a fall of ninety-nine percent.
    draw endpt drop

Why 1989? That year the Montreal Protocol came into force, to phase out CFCs from fridges and spray cans.
    draw montreal

In time every country in the United Nations signed it, the first treaty ever to manage that.
    draw every

    erase axes line_1 endpt drop montreal every

They moved fast because, in 1985, scientists had found a hole in the ozone over Antarctica, letting through the ultraviolet light that causes skin cancer.
    draw tl mt1 holeic ml1

And it worked: around 2000, the hole stopped growing.
    draw mt2 ml2

But the old gases linger in the sky for decades. The hole over Antarctica should heal only around 2066.
    draw mt3 now ml3

So a few years of action stopped the damage, but the sky needs another forty years to heal.
    draw brace yrs40

